    "shift": "shift_1"
  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Glycerin of density <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> is flowing through the conical section of pipe. The area of cross-section of the pipe at its ends are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;and pressure drop across its length is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The rate of flow of glycerine through the pipe is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is _____.</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0050_d6ed74721cce.png\" style=\"width: 450px; height: 212px;\" /></p><p>It is given that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>By continuity equation,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>By Bernoulli&#39;s equation,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>&#961;</mi><msup><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>&#961;</mi><msup><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Using equation (i) in (ii)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#961;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>(</mo><msub><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#961;</mi><msub><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><msub><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>So, the discharge rate is,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p>"
  }
}